            <ArticleTitle>Nonspecific low back pain: evaluation and treatment tips.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>445-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Avoid imaging in cases of uncomplicated low back pain (unless there are specific clinical indications). Use acetaminophen, nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, or muscle relaxants for short-term relief of acute nonspecific low back pain. Consider matching specific physical therapy options to the patient's history and exam findings.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
